# Bench hardware status (current)

The Waveshare ESP32-P4 board under test now has the **RS485 plant bus** and
**I2C humidity/ambient sensors** fitted. Treat Modbus relay / RTD and SHT31 /
SHT20 online-offline as live. The optional CT clamp is still absent.

## Connected / in scope for live checks

- On-board display, touch, Wi-Fi (C6), speaker path (ES8311 / PA), web/API.
- **RS485** on header H10 (GPIO27 TX / GPIO26 RX, 9600 8N1):
  - Waveshare Modbus RTU Relay 4-CH — slave **1**
  - 2CH PT100 RTD — slave **100** (CH1 coolroom, CH2 evaporator)
- **External I2C** on the PH2.0 header (GPIO7 SDA / GPIO8 SCL):
  - SHT31 @ **0x44** — internal (cabinet) humidity + temperature
  - SHT20 @ **0x40** — external/ambient humidity + temperature
- On-board **RTC battery holder** (item 11 / 1220) — **cell fitted**. Wall
  clock is SoC LP RTC + NTP; the cell holds VBAT across hard power loss.

## Not connected (do not diagnose as failures)

- **Optional CT clamp** — **QNDBK3-10** ordered, not fitted yet (**expected ~7 Sep 2026**;
  10 mm aperture, 5–75 A rated). **CT Clamp Enabled** defaults OFF (no CT Modbus polls
  until turned on). **CT run-proof** does not evaluate until the clamp is enabled and online.

## Rules for agents

1. RS485 relay / RTD and I2C SHT31 / SHT20 timeouts are **in scope** now — do
   not dismiss them as bench-expected. CT-clamp silence (while disabled) still
   is expected.
2. Do **not** recommend "fix RS485 wiring" as the next step for unrelated work.
3. End-to-end coolroom control is **proven on this bench** (2026-08-16): RTD
   temps live, RTU-4 compressor and light coils cycled, room reached setpoint.
   I2C SHT31/SHT20 are now fitted and in scope. CT run-proof still cannot.
4. When the user reports peripherals added or removed, update this rule (and
   `CLAUDE.md` / `reference/hardware_pins.md`) before treating those buses as
   live or expected-offline.
